C. Differences Between User Levels
An analysis of the subjective evaluation data of all evaluated variants separated by user level shows that in the ﬁrst questionnaire (BI) the entire sample shows signiﬁcant mean value differences in the same criteria as the subgroups of experts and non-experts. The results do not show signiﬁcant mean value differences in any of the evaluation items related to stationary steering feedback.
