D. Effect of Simulator Variations on Subjective Evaluations
T-tests for both modiﬁcations that were in effect between the simulator variants were performed for all criteria that showed signiﬁcant differences in the ANOVA. Since the modiﬁcations can be treated as independent factors applied to the simulator variants and each subject provided evaluations for combinations of both modiﬁcations, an independent sample t-test was chosen. Data following a normal distribution were analyzed with Student’s t-test when homogeneity of variances was given and Welch’s t-test else. Non-normal distributed data was analyzed through a Mann-Whitney U-test when homogeneity of variances was given and Yuen’s robust t-test else.

